<https://biocontainers.pro/tools/estscan> a ns1:SoftwareApplication ;
    ns1:citation "doi:10.1093/nar/29.1.148",
        "doi:10.1093/nar/gkh479",
        "doi:10.1093/nar/gkm352",
        "doi:10.1186/1751-0473-2-2" ;
    ns1:conformsTo "https://bioschemas.org/profiles/ComputationalTool/1.0-RELEASE" ;
    ns1:description "Estscan can detect coding regions (cds) in dna sequences, even if they are of low quality.  it  also detects/corrects sequencing errors that lead to frameshifts.  estscan is not a gene prediction program , nor is it an open reading frame detector.  in fact, its strength lies in the fact that it does not require an open reading frame to detect a coding region.  the program may miss a few translated amino acids at termini, but detects coding regions with high selectivity and sensitivity." ;
