<https://biocontainers.pro/tools/r-sqldf> a ns1:SoftwareApplication ;
    ns1:conformsTo "https://bioschemas.org/profiles/ComputationalTool/1.0-RELEASE" ;
    ns1:description "The sqldf() function is typically passed a single argument which is an SQL select statement where the table names are ordinary R data frame names. sqldf() transparently sets up a database, imports the data frames into that database, performs the SQL select or other statement and returns the result using a heuristic to determine which class to assign to each column of the returned data frame. The sqldf() or read.csv.sql() functions can also be used to read filtered files into R even if the original files are larger than R itself can handle. RSQLite, RH2, RMySQL and RPostgreSQL backends are supported." ;
    ns1:license "GPL-2.0" ;
    ns1:name "r-sqldf" ;
    ns1:provider <https://biocontainers.pro> ;
    ns1:url "https://github.com/ggrothendieck/sqldf" .

<https://biocontainers.pro/tools/r-stampp> a ns1:SoftwareApplication ;
    ns1:citation "doi:10.1111/1755-0998.12129" ;
    ns1:conformsTo "https://bioschemas.org/profiles/ComputationalTool/1.0-RELEASE" ;
    ns1:description "Allows users to calculate pairwise Nei's Genetic Distances (Nei 1972), pairwise Fixation Indexes (Fst) (Weir & Cockerham 1984) and also Genomic Relationship matrixes following Yang et al. (2010) in mixed and single ploidy populations. Bootstrapping across loci is implemented during Fst calculation to generate confidence intervals and p-values around pairwise Fst values. StAMPP utilises SNP genotype data of any ploidy level (with the ability to handle missing data) and is coded to utilise multithreading where available to allow efficient analysis of large datasets. StAMPP is able to handle genotype data from genlight objects allowing integration with other packages such adegenet." ;
    ns1:keywords "Computational Biology",
        "Genetics, Population",
        "Genotype",
        "Ploidies",
        "Polymorphism, Single Nucleotide" ;
    ns1:license "GPL-3.0" ;
    ns1:name "r-stampp" ;
    ns1:provider <https://biocontainers.pro> ;
    ns1:url "https://CRAN.R-project.org/package=StAMPP" .

